    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90837" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρυμν-ήσιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a stern</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					479
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> mostly neut.
			pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρυμνήσια</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεσμά</span>), <i>stern-cables</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ . . π. ἔδησαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.436
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάψαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.137
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνά . . π. λῦσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.178
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.418
			</span></i>, al.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν σοὶ τἀμὰ βίου πρυμνήσι᾽ ἀνῆπται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.159
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>),  cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Berol.</u>
				1.346
			</span></i>.</div>
